.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH terminal-of-tinsel-creature 1  "creature " 
.SH NAME
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-creature \- Tune in to the Midwinter Special, or read one creature\*(Aqs page
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBterminal\-of\-tinsel creature\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-reveal\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-x\fR|\fB\-\-explore\fR] [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-pack\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-intro\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fINAME\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
With no name, opens the Midwinter Special: an interactive explorer of every creature, with a gallery, numbered sections, portraits and search. Press ? inside it for the keys.
.PP
With a name, prints that creature\*(Aqs page. Nicknames and parts of names work, and accents are optional. Add \-\-explore to open the explorer on that creature instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the command\*(Aqs data as JSON instead of drawing it (errors become a JSON object on stderr)
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-reveal\fR
Show the verdicts in Myth or Fact?
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Plain output: no colour, no emoji, ASCII borders (also set by NO_COLOR, or by piping)
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-explore\fR
Open the explorer on the named creature instead of printing its page
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-all\fR
Open the explorer on the gallery of every creature
.TP
\fB\-\-pack\fR \fI<PACK>\fR
Only use creatures from these packs, e.g. \-\-pack nordic,dickens
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-intro\fR
Skip Channel 25 tuning in
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fINAME\fR]
The creature\*(Aqs name, nickname or part of one, e.g. krampus, "yule cat", nisse
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  terminal\-of\-tinsel creature
  terminal\-of\-tinsel creature krampus
  terminal\-of\-tinsel creature yule cat \-\-reveal
  terminal\-of\-tinsel creature marley \-\-explore
  terminal\-of\-tinsel creature marley \-\-json
